WHAT THIS COVERS
===========================================================================

A public domain dedication can only give away what the dedicator owns, so
it is worth being exact about what that is here.

COVERED — the work of this repository:

    tools/          the build, the AVR32 encoder, the transpiler, the tests
    src/            the Ghidra scripts, including the patch assembler
    docs/           the documentation
    config/         the build options
    calibration/    measurements taken from one specific instrument
    tunings/        Scala files written or adapted here
    ProgramLEM218_PressureFix.command   the updater script

NOT COVERED — the bundled flashing tools, each of which keeps its own
licence.  dfu-programmer and SendMIDI on both platforms, Zadig on Windows,
libusb, and the Microsoft C++ runtime.  Their presence does not place them in
the public domain and nothing here attempts to relicense them; if you
redistribute this tree, those files travel under their own terms.

THIRD-PARTY.md lists every one of them with its licence, its upstream project
and a written offer for the corresponding source.

NOT PRESENT — the firmware itself:

No firmware image is distributed from this repository.  The Buchla 218e
firmware is not ours to give away, and the patched image is that same
firmware with our changes spliced into it, so it is not ours to give away
either.  Both are excluded in .gitignore.

What is dedicated here is the recipe: the analysis, the patch sources, the
assembler and the build.  Supply your own factory image — you already have
it if you have the official flashing kit — and it will produce the patched
one locally.

